title: LSP Go to Definition

Ctrl-click a link and the editor opens the `.tid` file that holds its target, through `textDocument/definition`. Try it in [[LSP Go to Definition - (Example)]].

!! What can be followed

A `[[link]]`, a `{{transclusion}}` and a `<$link to="...">` widget all resolve. A transclusion of one field, such as `{{Title!!field}}`, opens the tiddler that holds the field.

!! Where the file comes from

The file comes from the map ~TiddlyWiki itself uses to save a tiddler, so a filename that differs from the title, a ~FileSystemPaths subfolder and a `.meta` sidecar all resolve.

!! When nothing opens

A shadow tiddler has no file of its own, so ctrl-click reports nothing rather than opening the wrong thing. Neither does a link to a tiddler that does not exist, nor a title merely mentioned in prose, which is no link at all.
